At Mon, 09 Jul 2007 08:07:19 -0700,
Tobin Davis wrote:
> 
> Sorry for missing this thread.  I just woke up.
> 
> I looked at your first pastebin output, and the actual audio codec shows up as
> 0x51d41981, when it should be 0x11d41981.  This is why the Analog driver patch isn't
> detecting it.

Ah, good catch.

> Can you try this patch against alsa-driver-1.0.14?  It should detect this codec. 
> Still not sure why it is misconfigured, unless there is a bios issue.

Yes, I guess it's some breakage in the BIOS, or possibly a problem of
RAM.  Since I've never heard of this problem, I highly suspect it's
Xavi's hardware-specific problem.  A memory test via memtest is
recommended.


